#N canvas 40 60 1250 1260 one-step 0;
#X text 20 10 ONE 16TH NOTE of the drummer ([r \$0-step] \, one bang per 16th). Each drum d has 16 weights th<d>\$0 (one per step) \, a memory e<d>\$0 and the policy p<d>\$0 (for the pictures). d = k s h r: kick \, snare \, hat \, rim. Every [t b b ...] fires from right to left., f 170;
#X obj 1040 70 array define thk\$0 16;
#X obj 1040 96 array define ths\$0 16;
#X obj 1040 122 array define thh\$0 16;
#X obj 1040 148 array define thr\$0 16;
#X text 1040 176 <- the weights theta of kick \, snare \, hat and rim (taste \, policy and memory are the graphs), f 28;
#X obj 460 70 r \$0-step;
#X obj 460 100 t b b b b b;
#X text 570 100 <- steps 1) to 5) \, right outlet first. Every [spigot 1] closes while practising., f 50;
#X text 20 160 1) NEXT STEP: t = 0 .. 15 (the bar starts at 0), f 52;
#X obj 460 160 expr t_\$0 = (t_\$0 + 1) % 16;
#X text 20 210 2) THE POLICY FIRES: p = sigmoid(theta / T) for this step \, then each drum hits (x = 1) with probability p. The randomness IS the exploration., f 52;
#X obj 460 210 t b b;
#X obj 520 240 expr p0_\$0 = 1 / (1 + exp(-thk\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; p1_\$0 = 1 / (1 + exp(-ths\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; p2_\$0 = 1 / (1 + exp(-thh\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; p3_\$0 = 1 / (1 + exp(-thr\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)), f 100;
#X obj 460 320 expr x0_\$0 = random(0 \, 1000000) < p0_\$0 * 1000000 \; x1_\$0 = random(0 \, 1000000) < p1_\$0 * 1000000 \; x2_\$0 = random(0 \, 1000000) < p2_\$0 * 1000000 \; x3_\$0 = random(0 \, 1000000) < p3_\$0 * 1000000, f 100;
#X text 20 410 3) THE MEMORY (eligibility trace): every e fades by lambda \, then this step adds what was done minus what was expected \, x - p: +0.7 for a surprising hit \, -0.7 for a surprising rest. A clap pays this memory., f 52;
#X obj 460 410 t b b;
#X obj 520 440 t b b;
#X msg 580 466 0;
#X msg 520 466 16;
#X obj 520 492 until;
#X obj 520 518 f;
#X obj 570 518 + 1;
#X obj 520 550 expr ek\$0[\$f1] = lam_\$0 * ek\$0[\$f1] \; es\$0[\$f1] = lam_\$0 * es\$0[\$f1] \; eh\$0[\$f1] = lam_\$0 * eh\$0[\$f1] \; er\$0[\$f1] = lam_\$0 * er\$0[\$f1], f 90;
#X obj 460 630 expr ek\$0[t_\$0] = ek\$0[t_\$0] + x0_\$0 - p0_\$0 \; es\$0[t_\$0] = es\$0[t_\$0] + x1_\$0 - p1_\$0 \; eh\$0[t_\$0] = eh\$0[t_\$0] + x2_\$0 - p2_\$0 \; er\$0[t_\$0] = er\$0[t_\$0] + x3_\$0 - p3_\$0, f 100;
#X text 20 720 4) THE DANCER (when switched on) pays right away: r = average over the drums of (2x - 1)(2 taste - 1) \, +1 for what it likes \, -1 for the opposite. REINFORCE: theta += rate * r * (x - p) / T \, only for this step. Then redraw the 4 probabilities of this step., f 52;
#X obj 460 720 t b b b;
#X obj 560 750 expr rc_\$0 = dan_\$0 * ((2 * x0_\$0 - 1) * (2 * min(max(tak\$0[t_\$0] \, 0) \, 1) - 1) + (2 * x1_\$0 - 1) * (2 * min(max(tas\$0[t_\$0] \, 0) \, 1) - 1) + (2 * x2_\$0 - 1) * (2 * min(max(tah\$0[t_\$0] \, 0) \, 1) - 1) + (2 * x3_\$0 - 1) * (2 * min(max(tar\$0[t_\$0] \, 0) \, 1) - 1)) / 4, f 90;
#X obj 510 814 expr thk\$0[t_\$0] = thk\$0[t_\$0] + lr_\$0 * rc_\$0 * (x0_\$0 - p0_\$0) / temp_\$0 \; ths\$0[t_\$0] = ths\$0[t_\$0] + lr_\$0 * rc_\$0 * (x1_\$0 - p1_\$0) / temp_\$0 \; thh\$0[t_\$0] = thh\$0[t_\$0] + lr_\$0 * rc_\$0 * (x2_\$0 - p2_\$0) / temp_\$0 \; thr\$0[t_\$0] = thr\$0[t_\$0] + lr_\$0 * rc_\$0 * (x3_\$0 - p3_\$0) / temp_\$0, f 100;
#X obj 460 894 expr pk\$0[t_\$0] = 1 / (1 + exp(-thk\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; ps\$0[t_\$0] = 1 / (1 + exp(-ths\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; ph\$0[t_\$0] = 1 / (1 + exp(-thh\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)) \; pr\$0[t_\$0] = 1 / (1 + exp(-thr\$0[t_\$0] / temp_\$0)), f 100;
#X text 20 994 5) TELL: print the step (exrl-trace 1) \, play the hits \, move the playheads. Sound and pictures are closed while practising., f 52;
#X obj 460 994 t b b b;
#X obj 1000 1024 expr t_\$0 \; x0_\$0 \; x1_\$0 \; x2_\$0 \; x3_\$0 \; p0_\$0 \; p1_\$0 \; p2_\$0 \; p3_\$0 \; rc_\$0, f 20;
